10
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
Immortal Beloved is a 1994 biographical film written and directed by Bernard Rose and
starring Gary Oldman, Jeroen Krabbé, Isabella Rossellini and Johanna ter Steege.

11
01:28:44,000 --> 01:28:50,000
The film narrates the life of composer Ludwig van Beethoven (played by Oldman) in flashbacks while it follows Beethoven's secretary and first biographer Anton Schindler's
(Krabbé) quest to ascertain the true identity of the Unsterbliche Geliebte (Immortal Beloved) addressed in three letters found in the late composer's private papers.

12
01:36:48,000 --> 01:36:54,000
Schindler journeys throughout the Austrian Empire interviewing women who might be
potential candidates, as well as through Beethoven's own tumultuous life.

13
01:44:52,000 --> 01:44:58,000
The film explores themes of composer, deaf, letter, biography, sister-in-law.

14
01:52:56,000 --> 01:53:02,000
The tone is emotional.
